---
description: How changes are made in this repository (builds, tests, PRs). Applies to every task.
alwaysApply: true
---

Before changing anything, read `AGENTS.md` at the repository root and follow it. In short:

- Branch from the latest `origin/main` (`cursor/<topic>`); never push to `main` or to `ccr-*` branches.
- Edit `src/`, never `index.html`; regenerate it with `node tools/build.mjs`.
- One PR = one build: `node tools/stamp.mjs` once per PR; if main moves, merge it (no rebase), re-stamp and rebuild.
- Physics is derived from cited sources, never fitted to pass a test; record and compare `tools/fingerprint.mjs`.
- Every change adds or updates `tests/testNNN.mjs` (WHY THIS EXISTS header, exit code); never skip or loosen tests.
- Every visible string has Greek (`tr()` + `I18N`); run `node tests/run.mjs 87` on UI changes.
- CHANGELOG entry `### <title> (build N)`; commit and PR titled `Build N: <title>`; the owner merges (squash) and tags.
